# tally 2.2.1 (#214, 214.1), E §4.1 step 2: a window-dated movement "makes bal(x, d) a hole for d inside the window,
# but for a leg of amount 0" (L §5.14: "an amount of 0 books nothing"); L §4.4: "a window of one day is that day". one
# (amount 0 PLN, a window of one day) and nul (amount amt - amt) book nothing on any day, so sav is 0.00 PLN inside
# both windows and after them, with no hole and no unknown day. tally 2.2 gave the hole naming w0 and w1 on every day
# after the windows began (the planner's misc/m1.tally, asks oneday and zerowin).
=== m.tally
model m1
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input w1: date
input w0: date
move one: transfers
  on w1
  leg cash from world to sav amount 0 PLN
move nul: transfers
  on w0
  leg cash from world to sav amount amt - amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  w1 = window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-10) "s"
  w0 = window(2026-03-12, 2026-03-14) "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
ask oneday: bal(sav, 2026-03-31)
ask zerowin: bal(sav, 2026-03-13)
ask inday: bal(sav, 2026-03-10)
=== expect
inday: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-10
oneday: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-10
zerowin: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-10
